// A place the world won't take says why in one short line, the way a refused dig does: a brick in mid-air
// ("Can't place brick: needs something to rest on."), a brick into the rock floor (something is in the way),
// a table or cart the pack has none of, a torch into rock or, in Survival, with no fungus oil left to light
// it. The same words aren't said again for 5 s however often you click; a different reason speaks at once.
map
BBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBB
B............................B
B............................B
B............................B
B............................B
B............................B
B............................B
B............................B
B............................B
B.....@......................B
##############################
BBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBB
end
mode survival
give Brick 20
brush 1 0.5
place 10 4 -6 Brick
place 12 4 -6 Brick
place 14 5 -6 Brick
expect 15 log:needs_something_to_rest_on == 1
expect 15 log:can't_place_brick == 1
place 20 4 2 Brick
expect 21 log:something_is_in_the_way == 1
expect 21 log:can't_place == 2
furnish 30 Table 4 0
expect 31 log:can't_place_table == 1
place 40 4 -6 Cart
expect 41 log:cart:_none == 1
expect 41 log:none_left == 2
placetorch 50 3 1
expect 51 log:can't_place_torch == 1
expect 51 log:something_is_in_the_way == 2
placetorch 60 2 0
placetorch 62 3 0
placetorch 64 4 0
placetorch 66 5 0
expect 67 log:fungus_oil == 1
placetorch 68 5 0
expect 69 log:fungus_oil == 1
place 420 4 -6 Brick
expect 421 log:needs_something_to_rest_on == 2
place 422 4 -6 Brick
expect 423 log:needs_something_to_rest_on == 2
